WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
Speaker 1: We're right in the middle of a very&nbsp;
interesting and globally significant story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:10.720
whose details are changing so quickly that by the&nbsp;
time today's episode goes live, you may actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.440
know more than I know right now. And it has to&nbsp;
do with Nancy Pelosi, the Speaker of the House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:23.760
in the United States, the country of China and&nbsp;
Taiwan, and understanding some of the history of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.800
the United States, China and Taiwan is important&nbsp;
to understanding what's going on, which we will,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:36.320
of course, get to to begin with. The big story is&nbsp;
Nancy Pelosi is was at least as of this morning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:44.720
expected to visit Taiwan, according to Taiwanese&nbsp;
and United States officials. And as CNN says,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:52.640
Nancy Pelosi is on a tour of Asia. And despite&nbsp;
warnings from Biden administration officials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:59.360
and from China, Nancy Pelosi is&nbsp;
believed to be heading to Taiwan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:06.400
This is certainly controversial when it comes to&nbsp;
China because of the policy of the United States&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:16.400
of at least for foreign relations and geopolitical&nbsp;
negotiation purposes. Recognizing China and China&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:23.280
alone, although the U.S. has supported Taiwanese&nbsp;
membership in a number of different coalitions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:30.960
and organizations over the years, sort of staking&nbsp;
out not what I would call a 5050 position on China&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:37.040
and Taiwan, but certainly not a policy that is as&nbsp;
extreme and reactionary as what China would want,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:43.040
which is to pretend that there is no such thing,&nbsp;
even as Taiwan sort of out in the world. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:50.480
would be, as the CNN article says, the first stop&nbsp;
in Taiwan for a U.S. House speaker in 25 years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.960
It is not currently on Pelosi's public itinerary.&nbsp;
And this is being interpreted one of two ways.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:02.320
One way in which this is being interpreted is&nbsp;
they've decided to bail on the Taiwan visit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:09.040
The counterpoint is, well, it just was never&nbsp;
on the itinerary. So it's a signal that she may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:14.880
still plan to do it, but it's at least not being&nbsp;
given the same sort of position and significance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:21.280
that other visits are being given by virtue of&nbsp;
not being placed on the official itinerary. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.320
Taiwanese official added that Pelosi is expected&nbsp;
to stay in Taiwan overnight. It's unclear when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.960
she would be in Taipei. The U.S. official added&nbsp;
that Defense Department officials are working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:36.400
around the clock on monitoring Chinese movements&nbsp;
and securing a plan to keep Nancy Pelosi safe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:46.880
China has issued warnings saying the military will&nbsp;
not stand idly by. If Nancy Pelosi visits Taiwan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.920
now. The least. I don't know if charitable&nbsp;
is the right word to use here, but the least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:57.600
charitable or most aggressive interpretation of&nbsp;
this comment would be that the Chinese military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:04.720
would target Nancy Pelosi specifically. That does&nbsp;
not seem to be the consensus opinion right now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.120
But there's a lot of questions around what's&nbsp;
going on. This is a Reuters report which says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.440
the latest warning was issued&nbsp;
during a Chinese foreign ministry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:22.560
regular briefing. Spokesperson Zhao Lijian&nbsp;
also said that because of Pelosi's status as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:28.560
the number three official of the U.S. government,&nbsp;
a visit to Taiwan, which China claims as its own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:36.880
would, quote, lead to egregious political impact.&nbsp;
Pelosi was set to kick off a tour of four Asian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:44.400
countries Monday in Singapore, with speculation&nbsp;
that she risks the wrath of Beijing by visiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:52.960
Self-Ruled Taiwan. This is a very interesting&nbsp;
geopolitical story and also potentially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:58.640
of significant consequence because US-China&nbsp;
relations are not particularly strong right now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:06.160
Donald Trump, by virtue of his what do we even&nbsp;
call it, belligerent posturing about Taiwan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:13.920
about China, rather, has arguably sunk those&nbsp;
relations to a new low. A year of talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:20.640
about the China virus certainly didn't help. And&nbsp;
although things have not further escalated under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:26.240
Joe Biden, they certainly haven't been repaired in&nbsp;
any significant way. The official position of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:33.360
United States when it comes to China policy is&nbsp;
not overtly supporting Taiwanese independence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:37.600
but supporting Taiwanese membership in some&nbsp;
international organizations. That includes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:42.960
WTO. The U.S. says, okay, we don't recognize&nbsp;
Taiwan's independence, but we recognize that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:47.760
Taiwan as an entity should be part of the World&nbsp;
Trade Organization. Well, usually it's countries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:53.600
that are members of that, so it creates this kind&nbsp;
of arguably deliberately nebulous situation. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:59.840
U.S. has supported Taiwanese membership in the&nbsp;
Asia-Pacific Pacific Economic Cooperation Forum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.160
the Asian Development Bank. Now, you&nbsp;
don't need to be an independent state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:10.640
to be a member of the Asian Development Bank.&nbsp;
So it's a, generally speaking, pro-China policy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:17.200
that is not pro-China enough for China. And we&nbsp;
will see what happens here. We will see what Nancy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:23.200
Pelosi ultimately does. And probably in the next&nbsp;
24 to 48 hours, we will have more news about it.

